# API CommonJS Conventions

## Style

- Code is **CommonJS** (`.cjs`). Do not convert modules to ESM unless explicitly asked.
- HTTP uses raw Node `http` (no Express). Follow existing `canHandle*` / `tryHandle*` / `deps` injection patterns.
- Prefer extending existing modules under `apps/api/src/modules/` rather than inventing new top-level frameworks.

## Layout

| Concern | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Main server / routes | `src/modules/api-console/infrastructure/http/` |
| Persistence adapters | `src/modules/api-console/infrastructure/persistence/` |
| Vault / prod secrets | `src/modules/api-console/infrastructure/security/` |
| Session / CSRF | `src/modules/session/` |
| Local auth | `src/modules/auth/` |
| CDE / SSO | `src/modules/cde/` |
| Runtime Core | `src/modules/runtime/` |
| Workspace gate | `src/modules/access/` |
| IS (frozen) | `src/modules/is/` — regression fixes only |
| OpenAPI | `src/openapi/` |
| Prisma | `prisma/` |

## Tests

- Tests are `node --test` under `apps/api/test/*.cjs`.
- Prefer the matching script in `apps/api/package.json` (e.g. `test:session`, `test:vault`) over inventing new runners.
- Keep IS flag tests asserting disabled-by-default behavior.

## Safety

- Destination validation / SSRF policy must not be weakened without explicit human approval.
- Surgical edits only to `api-console-server.cjs`.
